## 4. Existing audio/video/media/asset components — confirmed: none

Exhaustive grep for `AUDIO|VIDEO|MEDIA|Audio|Video|Media|audio|video|media` across `spec/`, `pathland-core`, the renderers, the TS client, and `lib/java` returns only:

- `css.rs:51` — the UA reset selector `img, svg, video, canvas, audio, iframe, embed, object` (a generic CSS reset, not a component).
- `@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)` CSS queries in `css.rs` / token handling — unrelated.
- `jakarta.ws.rs.core.MediaType` / `org.springframework.http.MediaType` imports in the starters — HTTP content-type constants, unrelated.

There is **no `AUDIO`, `VIDEO`, `MEDIA`, `IMAGE_*` beyond `IMAGE_SOURCE`/`CONTENT_MODE`**, no component ID allocated (the primitive range 0x01–0x0F has 0x09–0x0F reserved — `constants.rs:222`), and no renderer arm, no DSL type. The component-type map (`constants.rs:204–273`) and property map end at `COLOR_PICKER`/`COMMENT`. Your assumption is correct: **audio/video have zero protocol surface today.**

