## 5. Java DSL Image API + Label/icon usage in Sidebar

### Image API (see full quote in §1e)
- Factories: `Image.of()`, `Image.of(String source)`, `Image.of(Signal<String> source)`.
- `render()` maps to `PathlandNode(Components.IMAGE)` and writes `Properties.IMAGE_SOURCE` either statically or as a bound signal (`node.propertyBindings`).
- Modifiers typically used on images: `ImageSource.of(String)` (explicit modifier), `AspectRatio.of(float, ContentMode)`, `ScaledToFit.of()`, `ScaledToFill.of()`, plus generic `FrameMod.of(...)`, `Opacity`, `CornerRadius`, `Clipped`, etc.

### `Label` — `lib/java/pathland-view/src/main/java/com/pathland/view/Label.java`
`Label` is the composite through which all demo icons flow (`Label.java:69–94`):
```java
List<View> children = new ArrayList<>(2);
if (nonBlank(icon) && style.showsIcon()) {
    children.add(iconSignal != null ? Image.of(iconSignal) : Image.of(icon));
}
if (nonBlank(title) && style.showsTitle()) {
    View text = titleSignal != null ? Text.of(titleSignal) : Text.of(title);
    children.add(text.modifier(LineLimit.of(1)));
}
View stack = HStack.of(Alignment.CENTER, 2f, children);
if (nonBlank(title)) {
    stack = stack.modifier(titleSignal != null
            ? AccessibilityLabel.of(titleSignal)
            : AccessibilityLabel.of(title));
}
```
So `Label.of(title, icon)` → `HStack[Image(icon), Text(title)]` with an `AccessibilityLabel` (→ `Properties.LABEL`) on the wrapper. `Label.of(title, icon)` has signal overloads for both title and icon (`Label.java:39–67`).

### Sidebar usage — `Sidebar.java:50–61`
```java
private View menuRow(String path, String label, String icon) {
    ...
    return Button.of(
            Label.of(label, icon).modifiers(Background.of(bg), ForegroundStyle.of(fg)),
            () -> router.navigate(path)
    );
}
```
The icon string is passed through verbatim into `Image.of(icon)` inside `Label`, then onto the wire as `IMAGE_SOURCE`.

