## 7. Value-type mapping for IMAGE_SOURCE (STRING)

**Rust** — `pathland_core::constants::value_type_for` (constants.rs:497–531), STRING arm at 519–523:
```rust
property_id::LABEL
| property_id::PROMPT
| property_id::FONT_FAMILY
| property_id::IMAGE_SOURCE
| property_id::ROUTE => value_type::STRING,
```
(`value_type::STRING = 0x05`, constants.rs:192.)

**Java** — `ValueTypes.forProperty` (`ValueTypes.java:26–27`):
```java
case Properties.LABEL, Properties.PROMPT, Properties.FONT_FAMILY, Properties.IMAGE_SOURCE,
        Properties.ROUTE -> STRING;
```
The Java emitter derives the wire type this way — `Emitter.emitProperty` (`Emitter.java:246–251`):
```java
private void emitProperty(int nodeId, int property, Object value) {
    int valueType = value instanceof Color c && c.isToken()
            ? ValueTypes.DESIGN_TOKEN
            : ValueTypes.forProperty(property);
    sink.setProperty(nodeId, property, valueType, value);
}
```
`FrameOpcodeSink.setProperty` (`FrameOpcodeSink.java:84–98`) then serializes a STRING into the frame's string section and puts the **relative offset** in `C`:
```java
if (valueType == ValueTypes.STRING) {
    int offset = strings.size();
    writeString((String) value);
    push(Categories.STYLE, Commands.Style.SET_PROPERTY, 0, nodeId, b, offset);
}
```
The canonical spec mapping is in `spec/MODIFIERS.md:378`: `LABEL, PROMPT, FONT_FAMILY, IMAGE_SOURCE, ROUTE → STRING`; allocation table at `spec/MODIFIERS.md:345/364`; the PRIMITIVES catalog at `spec/PRIMITIVES.md:250` documents `IMAGE_SOURCE` as "STRING: a resource name, file path, or absolute URL". The TS client mirrors the constants (`constants.ts:112`), and the DOM renderer's decoder treats `VAL_STRING` properties via `applyStringProperty` (`apply.ts:508–515`).

